        "description": "Reads specific paths from a YAML file.\nMore efficient than reading entire files when you only need certain values.\n\nPath is specified as an array of strings, e.g., [\"spec\", \"containers\", \"0\", \"image\"]\n- Keys are strings: [\"metadata\", \"name\"]\n- Array indices are strings: [\"items\", \"0\"]\n- Root (entire file): empty array []\n\nReturns the YAML subtree at each path. Useful for:\n- Checking current values before editing\n- Reading specific configuration values\n- Extracting parts of large YAML files\n\nThe order of the returned values matches the order of paths requested"
      },
      {
        "name": "ImplementScenarioTool",
        "description": "# ImplementScenarioTool\nThis tool is a composite of the edit yaml and verify scenario, it returns a string report of each\n# EditYaml\nEdits a YAML file using path-based operations. More efficient than text-based editing\nbecause you specify YAML paths instead of large find/replace strings.\n\nSupports three operations:\n- set: Sets a value at a path (creates intermediate nodes if needed)\n- delete: Removes a value at a path (WARNING: deleting array items will shift index values)\n- insert: Inserts a value into an array at an index, shifting existing elements\n\nPath is specified as an array of strings, e.g., [\"spec\", \"containers\", \"0\", \"image\"]\n- Keys are strings: [\"metadata\", \"name\"]\n- Array indices are strings: [\"items\", \"0\"]\n- Root (entire file): empty array []\n\nFor 'set' and 'insert' operations, you must specify:\n- valueType: \"object\", \"array\", \"scalar\", or \"null\"\n- value: The raw YAML content (not required for \"null\" type)\n\nFor 'insert' operations, the path must end with an array index.\n\nExamples:\n- Set scalar: path=[\"metadata\", \"name\"], valueType=\"scalar\", value=\"my-app\"\n- Set object: path=[\"spec\"], valueType=\"object\", value=\"{replicas: 3}\"\n- Set array: path=[\"items\"], valueType=\"array\", value=\"[a, b, c]\"\n- Set null: path=[\"metadata\", \"annotations\"], valueType=\"null\"\n- Insert at index 0: path=[\"items\", \"0\"], valueType=\"scalar\", value=\"new-first\"\n- Insert in middle: path=[\"steps\", \"2\"], valueType=\"object\", value=\"{name: new-step}\"\n\nThis tool supports multiple edits (one per operation entry in the operations list). It is recommended to\nALWAYS perform multiple edits in one tool call instead of calling one edit at a time, as this is slow\nand extremely wasteful on tokens passing context back and forth\n# VerifyScenario\nPerforms a sequence of real run -> real run to verify this scenario works and is repeatable, the\noutput of this tool is a markdown report that either confirms this scenario is correct and needs no more\nchanges, or it will provide details on where it is incorrect or failing\n\nWhen autoFixHttpAssertSteps is provided, the tool attempts to set the expected value and body_matcher on each\nHttpAssert step id provided by using the real outputs observed in the actual value. These fixes are persisted\nto the scenario and any changed fields are returned in the markdown report of this tool\n# ReadYaml\nIf edits were made, then the full new state of the scenario is returned"
